         TWO DISPOSITION ENTRIES ADDED 2026-08-09 (Tranche 3B). The four pre-existing entries
         are UNTOUCHED, byte for byte.

         ⚠ DYNAMIC ACTIONS WAS ALREADY ON HERE (enableActionsConfiguration = true) AND WAS NOT
         ENABLED ANYWHERE NEW. Turning it on a page where it is OFF silently EMPTIES that page's
         action bar - it discards every inherited action - which cost three pages their buttons
         in this repo. This edit only appends entries to a list that already existed.

         THE TWO NEW ENTRIES DRIVE THE SELL-SIDE NEGOTIATION LOOP. The disposition path is
         Received -> Under Review -> Countered by DPEG -> Counter Received from Buyer ->
         Executed, and the middle two are a CYCLE ("it goes round until both sides are agreed").
         A linear NEXT_STAGE map cannot express a back-edge, so each loop stage gets a button
         naming the other. See the two quickActions/LOI__c.Mark_* files for the full reasoning.

         🔴 THERE IS NO RECORD-TYPE CRITERION ON EITHER NEW ENTRY, AND THAT IS CORRECT RATHER
         THAN AN OMISSION. objects/LOI__c/recordTypes/*.recordType-meta.xml both record the
         load-bearing property that THE TWO STAGE VALUE SETS ARE FULLY DISJOINT - no Stage__c
         value appears on both record types - so a rule keyed on a stage value is SELF-LIMITING
         to its own record type. 'Countered by DPEG' and 'Counter Received from Buyer' exist
         ONLY on Disposition_LOI, so these buttons are structurally unreachable on an
         acquisition LOI. This is the same mechanism that lets the four acquisition entries
         (Prepare/Review, Sent) stay record-type-agnostic. ⚠ CONTRAST NDA__c, whose Sent and
         Signed ARE shared, which is why NDA_Record_Page needed Is_Decline_Allowed__c as an
         explicit discriminator and this page needs no equivalent. If a future change makes any
         LOI stage value shared across the two record types, EVERY rule on this page must be
         revisited.

         EVERY RULE IS A PURE CHAIN OF ANDs. A flexipage booleanFilter has no negation operator,
         and this repo has MEASURED that a parenthesised OR ('1 AND 2 AND (3 OR 4)') deploys,
         survives a retrieve, and is STILL NOT HONOURED BY THE RENDERER - the button stayed
         visible. Neither new entry needs an OR; if a future one does, express it as two
         separate valueListItems (the shape NDA_Record_Page introduced) rather than as an OR.

         ✅ THE 3B KNOWN GAP (D22) IS CLOSED HERE, 2026-08-09. LOI__c.Advance_Stage NOW HAS A
         SECOND ENTRY for the disposition persona. The gap was: the single entry was gated on
         {!$User.Deal_Driver__c} EQUAL true, and a disposition driver holds
         Disposition_Deal_Driver, which grants NO FLS on Deal_Driver__c - a visibility rule
         reading a field the running user cannot read evaluates FALSE - so that criterion could
         never be true for them, and there was no linear walk for Received -> Under Review or
         Counter Received from Buyer -> Executed. Same shape as D20/C1 on NDA_Record_Page.

         🔬 PHASE 1 UPDATE (2026-08-12) — the mechanism described above is HISTORICAL, not
         live. Both criteria on this page now read {!$Permission.CustomPermission.
         Acquisition_Deal_Actions} / {!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}
         instead of a User field, so the "grants NO FLS on Deal_Driver__c" failure mode this
         page's duplicate-entry shape exists to work around cannot recur here — a custom
         permission has no FLS to be missing. The DUPLICATE-ENTRY SHAPE ITSELF IS UNCHANGED
         and still required for the reason stated below (booleanFilter has no OR): each persona
         still needs its own entry, now gated by its own custom permission rather than its own
         flag. See agent-output/design-requirements-custom-permissions.md.

         ⚠ SECOND CORRECTION, 2026-08-19, TO THE SAME HISTORICAL PARAGRAPH. It also says "a
         disposition driver holds Disposition_Deal_Driver". THAT SET NO LONGER EXISTS - it was
